<title>MEXICO: Mexico outlines equity future packages for MexDer.</title>
<headline>Mexico outlines equity future packages for MexDer.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Mexican Stock Exchange said Monday it had defined which companies will be in the first three equity blocks to be traded as futures contracts in the exchange's upcoming derivative market, known as MexDer.  </p>
<p>Block One will be telephone company Telmex L shares, corn flour maker Grupo Industrial Maseca B series, steelmaker Ahmsa,  builder Empresas ICA and cement maker Cemex's B series. Each firm is the leading Mexican company in its sector.  </p>
<p>Block Two will be holding company Carso's A1 series, industrial giant Grupo Industrial Alfa A series, glass company Vitro, paper conglomerate Kimberly Clark de Mexico A series and cigarette manufacturer Empresas La Moderna A series.</p>
<p>Block Three will be chain store company Cifra B series, media giant Grupo Televisa's CPO series, bottler Femsa's B series, industrail holding Desc's B series and steel pipe maker Tamsa.</p>
<p>The equity blocks will trade on MexDer alongside futures contracts foreseen for the stock market's main IPC index, forex futures and interest rate futures. MexDer will officially start trading in October.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530))</p>
